WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.434
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.501
You look good, bud.
How's the fam?

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:04.868
How's --
-Good.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:07.734
Yeah, we're doing good.
She's -- Wednesday's nearly 3.

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:10.701
-Yeah. Are you proud of
the name Wednesday, seeing --

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:13.167
-Well, yeah, I know.
-Seeing the success of --

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:15.834
I mean, you timed that one out.
-Glad we kind of got in there.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.167
-You were ahead of the curve.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:18.467
-There's gonna be a boom,
a "Wednesday" boom.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.334
-Oh, everyone's gonna be named
Wednesday next year.

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:21.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:22.934
You crushed it!
-It's a good name.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.000
I stand by it.
-What is she interested in?

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.701
What is she into?
-Um, so many things.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:29.801
I mean, she's kind of
princess crazy, as well.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.434
But she's struggling
a little bit with kind of

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:35.067
adjusting to U.K. life.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:38.033
She spent most of her time
in America, so she's missing

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.701
some kind of cultural things --
-Did you film "Servant" here?

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:40.701
Is that --
-We did.

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:41.868
We filmed it in Philadelphia.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:44.033
So she's --
-Philly, so she loves Philly.

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:45.667
-She does love Philly.
She loves hoagies.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.467
She loves water ice.
-Yeah.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:48.634
[ Scattered cheers ]
-And, I mean, the big --

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:53.400
the big one -- Yeah.
The big one is Target.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.200
She is obsessed with Target.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.267
-It's unbelievable.
My kids, too.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.834
-Oh, really?
-Loved it!

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:04.701
-She'd choose that over going
to the park, the zoo.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.067
-Over Disney, anything.
"Let's go to Target."

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.033
-But she loves going
to different Targets

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.000
and kind of seeing how
the layout

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.701
is kind of slightly different.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.234
And sometimes
she doesn't buy anything.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:16.934
She just wants to kind of
browse.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:21.200
-At the toy aisles?
-The toy aisle is definitely

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.067
a draw, but she's more into
lip balm, to be fair.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.133
-She goes to
the lip balm section?

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.367
-Lip balm, yeah.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.067
-But she's so into Target
that you built a little

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.400
Target play store for her...
-Yeah, I did, yeah.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.767
-...in your house.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:35.501
-Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:37.934
Just, uh -- yeah.
I think I've -- I think I've

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.100
definitely captured the --
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.000
I've captured essence.
-Yeah, well, you have all

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.434
the gift cards there,
yeah, absolutely.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.501
-Gift cards, yeah.
-But she's tiny.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:48.000
How old is she, 2 1/2?
-She's 2 1/2, yeah, yeah.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.234
-So, what does she just roam
around and talk to everybody?

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.934
-Yeah, she's chatty.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:54.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.534
-I love that she loves Target.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.734
-It was one of the most
difficult conversations

00:01:57.734 --> 00:01:59.067
telling her that she lives
in a country

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:00.734
that doesn't have Target.
-Yeah.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.801
Yeah, U.K. does not have --
-We don't have it.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.234
I've shown her the kind of --
our equivalent,

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.834
but it just doesn't --
-It doesn't hold up?

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.200
No, no.
Well, Target, get on the ball.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.400
Go over -- Let's go --
Let's go global, yeah.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.701
We were talking.
I was like,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.601
"What's one of the first things
you ever bought?"

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.567
And I go, "When you got
your driver's license,

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.200
what was your car?"

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.167
And you had
a very interesting answer.

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.534
And I never thought
you were gonna say this,

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:27.467
but the first car that you
bought, you bought a truck.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:28.667
-I did, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.701
You bought an ice-cream truck.

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:35.133
Mr. Whippy.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:37.200
It's a great truck.
A great truck.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.667
-Is Mr. Whippy famous in...?

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:42.300
-Yeah, I don't believe --
I guess the equivalent --

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.901
It's Mr. Frosty is what --
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:48.934
-Yeah, it's kind of
an iconic soft serve.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.467
I've always loved the trucks.
-Yeah.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.901
-And it's something
I always wanted to have.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.701
It's nostalgic,
it's the music, it's --

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.701
I mean, it's the most
impractical first car.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.968
-It's a terrible first car.
-Because it has one seat,

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:03.033
and the rest of it is --
It's all freezer.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:04.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:07.667
-Where does it -- Where do you
even drive to take your test?

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:10.267
The teacher
can't be in the vehicle.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.534
-Yeah, I know.
I didn't actually --

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.133
-Take the test on the thing.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:16.467
-It was my everyday car
for a while.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:17.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.033
-You drove Mr. Whippy around?

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:21.000
-Yeah, I did.
But then it was --

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.501
I did feel a little bit
kind of creepy

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:25.601
driving an ice-cream van
with no ice cream in it.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.267
It never had any
ice cream in it.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.100
-You never used it
for ice cream?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.334
-No, the only time I ever did
was actually,

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:34.000
I took it
on the last day of filming

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.467
"Deathly Hallows: Part 2."

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:38.133
They had, like, a Mariachi band,
and I brought the van

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:41.767
to sell ice cream to the crew,
and -- yeah.

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.467
-So, you did use it.
-I did use it, yeah.

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:44.901
For those kind of events,
it's perfect.

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:47.467
-Is it hard to park this thing?
-It's impossible to park.

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.901
And also you have to be careful
where you park.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.901
Because other ice-cream men
are very territorial.

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:54.734
[ Laughter ]
It's dangerous.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.234
-It sounds
like a nightmare to me.

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:57.634
-It's kinda like a Mafia, yeah.
-It sounds like a nightmare.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.667
Before we talk about "Servant,"
I want to talk about --

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:02.834
mention your new film
coming out next month,

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.133
called "Knock at the Cabin."

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:06.767
No, no, no, I know.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.968
M. Night Shyamalan,
he's just a genius.

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:10.567
But, I mean,
it looks frightening.

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:14.300
I think the trailer got like
over 22 million views already

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.200
'cause people are freaking out,
scared about it.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.467
Are you getting
used to Night at all?

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.734
Like, and the twists and turns
that he does?

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.000
-Yeah, I am.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.834
I'm kind of getting more
kind of acclimatized to it.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.734
I love Night.
I've kind of got to know him

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.000
over the years.
-Did you know

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.667
he surprised me once,
just being in the audience

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:32.667
one night, didn't tell me?
-Yeah, I saw -- I saw that.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.300
-It was bizarre.
I was just walking in,

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.601
I go,
"Are you M. Night Shyamalan?"

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:39.634
He's like, "How you doing man?"
That's frightening.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:40.734
You can't just
be in the audience.

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:42.400
-That's classic.
It's classic Night.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.567
It's a twist.
It's a twist.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.000
-It's a twist on everything,
yeah.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.901
Let's talk about "Servant."
This is the fourth,

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:50.267
this is the final season.
Congrats on a great run.

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.200
But now,
the series coming to an end,

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.634
are there questions --
Will they be answered?

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:57.601
Or are they -- is there twisties
and turns in this?

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.300
-I mean, yeah,
there's a lot of questions

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:02.300
I think this season kind of
does its best to answer.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.968
And it's great.
It's so nice to be --

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:07.167
become a part of this show.
I love it, I love the cast.

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.701
It's been kind of the longest
thing I've been a part of

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:12.000
since "Potter,"
so it's a real family,

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.767
and it's --
-Is there anything we can do

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:15.100
to set up this last season,

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.467
or set up what's gonna happen,
or no?

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:19.167
-Again, it's really hard for me
to talk about.

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:22.067
I don't want to -- there's so
many kind of loose ends.

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:24.534
But it's a very satisfying
ending, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.234
-I'll take that.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:28.133
Here's Rupert Grint
in "Servant."

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:29.534
Take a look at this.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:32.133
-Fantastic, isn't it?

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:36.868
Her gifts grow every day.
You must be in awe.

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:39.033
-What are you talking about?

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:43.634
-She did this so protect us from
those who wish to do us harm.

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.400
Don't you see?

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.634
There's a war afoot.

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:51.767
She's shielding us,
shielding your family.

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.801
-God, you people
are something else.

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.300
Sorry to break it to you,
but I think it's more

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.701
of an issue of hygiene
and negligence, not voodoo.

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:01.934
-You can feel it, can't you?
When you're close to her,

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:04.334
there is something
that pulls you in,

00:06:04.334 --> 00:06:07.167
tells you that she is the way.

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:10.367
It's her power.

00:06:10.367 --> 00:06:11.701
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:14.467
Rupert Grint, everybody!
Season four of "Servant"

00:06:14.467 --> 00:06:17.234
premieres this Friday
on Apple TV+.

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:19.467
We'll be right back with a
performance from Dry Cleaning.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:20.968
Stick around, everybody.

